{
  "about": [
    "Stroke plans for the russian-cursive widget: for each letter, its strokes as S1 pieces (shapes.json names) in drawing order, read by build-strokes.js.",
    "Each stroke is a list of steps. A step names the evidence.json record it follows and copies that record's text word for word in 'evidence' (build-strokes.js checks it), gives the direction, and lists its pieces in order, each with 'reverse' (true draws the piece against its stored direction in shapes.json).",
    "follows: 'segments[N]' for a segment of the letter's evidence.json record, or one of joiningMarks.entry, joiningMarks.exit, openPoints, penLifts, structure.difference, structure.consequence.",
    "Every evidence segment is cited, in evidence order. Every S1 piece of the form is drawn. A piece drawn a second time sits in a step with 'retrace': true. Consecutive pieces meet within 0.01 S1 units.",
    "Entry and exit pieces are kept (the Batch 71 precedent for т): S1 inks the joining strokes that S2 shows as grey dotted lines.",
    "A plan may cut an S1 piece in 'splits', only where another piece of the form starts or ends on it (build-strokes.js checks the point lies on the piece within 0.01 S1 units); the halves are named <piece>/1 and <piece>/2. shapes.json is not changed.",
    "A step may cite several consecutive segments (lists in 'follows', 'evidence' and 'direction') when one S1 piece draws them all."
  ],
  "directions": {
    "ARROWED": "the cited segment's direction is shown by an arrow on S2 (copied from evidence.json)",
    "FORCED": "the cited segment's direction follows from its neighbours (copied from evidence.json)",
    "JOIN": "an entry or exit piece: S1 inks it, S2 shows it only as a grey dotted joining line; drawn into the letter (entry) or out of it (exit)",
    "INFERRED": "not recorded as a segment in evidence.json; the only continuation without a pen lift. Each one says why, for the owner's review"
  },
